<title>INDONESIA: Namibia, Indonesia sign energy, minerals pact.</title>
<headline>Namibia, Indonesia sign energy, minerals pact.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Namibia and Indonesia on Tuesday signed an agreement to work together in the exploration and processing of mineral and energy resources.</p>
<p>The memorandum of understanding was signed by visiting Namibian Mines and Energy Minister Andimba Toivo Ya Toivo and his Indonesian counterpart Ida Bagus Sudjana.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, the two countries would promote cooperation in mineral and energy resource development through their respective national agencies.</p>
<p>The pact will cover exploration, exploitation, processing and research and development.</p>
<p>Toivo Ya Toivo began a week-long visit to Indonesia on Monday.</p>
